{"ref":"BDB, נַ֫חְנוּ","hw":"נַ֫חְנוּ","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">נַ֫חְנוּ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">נָחְ֑נוּ</span></big>  <strong>pron. 1 pl. we (</strong>abbrev. from <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲנַחְנוּ</span>; cf. the forms <span dir=\"rtl\">نَحْنُ</span>, ንሕነ <span dir=\"rtl\">נַחְנָא</span>, just cited; also Assyrian <em>nîni</em><strong>)</strong> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 42:11\" href=\"/Genesis.42.11\">Gn 42:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:7\" href=\"/Exodus.16.7\">Ex 16:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 16:8\" href=\"/Exodus.16.8\">8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 32:32\" href=\"/Numbers.32.32\">Nu 32:32</a>; <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 3:42\" href=\"/Lamentations.3.42\">La 3:42</a>. (In <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:12\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.12\">2 S 17:12</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">נַחְנוּ</span> is 1 pl. perf. Qal from <span dir=\"rtl\">נוּחַ</span>.)","next":"BDB, אֲנָךְ","prev":"BDB, אֲנַ֫חְנוּ"}